//! Settled envelope rate tables of the ORG core 2 installer (derived values, no firmware bytes).
//!
//! Generated by `python tools/synth_env_rates.py emit` from
//! `docs/research/data/synth-env-rates-settled.csv`: the coefficient the installer
//! (`0x12720F..0x127281`) stores at `DM(0xC0E21 / 0E24 / 0E28)` for each signed index -64..64 (top
//! byte of an ADR strip word), read after the 16-pass refresh. Index `i` is at array position
//! `i + 64`. Decay and release hold the same table (equal at 129 of 129 indexes).
//!
//! VERIFIED: every word equals the oracle word of `python tools/synth_env_rates.py sweep` (poke at
//! pass 0, 64 passes, value constant over the last 32; test `tables_equal_the_settled_csv`),
//! amp, filter and oscillator chains agree. The old `fw_env_rates.rs` read 3 passes after the poke
//! and is stale at 104 of 129 indexes (docs/research/synth-env-rates-settled.md). Interpolation between
//! integer indexes is ASSUMED (the firmware reads integer indexes only).

